/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119835 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186119646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119835 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "0efe5b11-2c87-58e9-bf7c-e1eecb07adf2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120018 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120018 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120018 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120018 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120018 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120018 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120018 #edb/ref 1045 "The Cartesian Equation of a Plane" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120018 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186120715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120018 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120018 #edb/ref 1050 1080.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120018 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "80511d12-b7f3-5570-8b75-694c2aa3ad46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120715 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120715 #edb/ref 1061 17922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120715 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c247ca81-f4a5-53d1-8429-f69593877343" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120715 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120716 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120716 #edb/ref 1061 17923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120716 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7a8bd938-5945-5ebb-a062-1d4409d4ccd2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120716 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119832 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120717 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120717 #edb/ref 1061 17924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120717 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "38691512-c8ac-58b3-b639-597249a111ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120717 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120718 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120718 #edb/ref 1061 17925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120718 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4e18819d-30d0-5673-a2f4-2264aa09fbde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120718 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120719 #edb/ref 1061 17926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120719 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "311c08f2-aa3d-5ea5-8386-44e9771e47c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120719 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121050 #edb/ref 1064 "If we are given an equation of a plane using the dot product, we can always obtain an equation in terms of $x,$ $y,$ and $z.$ For example, suppose we have the plane that passes through the point $P(-7,5,-2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 3,-6,5 \\rangle.$\n\nFirst, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -7,5,-2 \\rangle,$ and we can write down the equation of the plane using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-6,5⟩ & =⟨-7,5,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-6,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-6,5⟩ & =-61\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation, we substitute $\\mathbf{r}=\\langle x,y,z \\rangle$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-6,5⟩ & =-61 \\\\ 3x-6y+5z & =-61 \\\\ 3x-6y+5z+61 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis final equation is called the **Cartesian equation of the plane**.\n\n![](images/77/77f18981dda500889655225eabbec730b7b295e6b16cec1700d56c2e27e0ac91.png)\n\nNote that in the equation \n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}3}x+({\\color{blue}-6})y+{\\color{blue}5}z+61 = 0,\n$$\n\nthe coefficients next to $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ are the coordinates of the normal vector \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\langle {\\color{blue}3},{\\color{blue}-6},{\\color{blue}5} \\rangle\n$$\n\n." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121050 #edb/re